Given that $K = \{1, 2, 3, \dots, 11\}$;

(i) list the prime numbers in $K$;

(ii) find the probability that a number selected at random from the set $K$ is not a prime number.

answer:
$(x + y)$ is common to both terms, so take it out:

$$
\begin{aligned}
(x + y)(2m - n) - m(x + y) &= (x + y)\left[(2m - n) - m\right] \\
&= (x + y)(m - n)
\end{aligned}
$$

> [!answer]
> {{green:$(x + y)(m - n)$}}

