The image of $P(2, 5)$ when translated by the vector $r$ is $(-3, 8)$. Find:

(i) $r$;

(ii) the image $Q'$ of $Q(-4, -6)$ when translated by $r$.

Joyce and Richard contributed GH₵ 10,000.00 and GH₵ 5,000.00 respectively to start a business. They agreed that Richard will be paid one-third of the profit as a manager and the rest of the profit will be shared in the ratio of their contributions. If the profit of GH₵ 9,000.00 was made, how much did:

(i) Joyce receive;

(ii) Richard receive in total?

The diagram shows the floor of a room with its dimensions. Find the;

(i) perimeter;

(ii) area;

(iii) cost of carpeting the floor if a carpet cost GH₵ 20.00 per square meter.

A painter places a ladder against a building at the window. The angle the foot of the ladder makes with the horizontal ground is $60^\circ$. If the distance from the foot of the ladder to the base of the building is 5 m;

(i) illustrate the information in a diagram;

(ii) find, correct to one decimal place, the;

$(\alpha)$ length of the ladder;

$(\beta)$ distance between the window and the foot of the building.

[Take $\tan 60^\circ = 1.732$ and $\cos 60^\circ = \dfrac{1}{2}$]

answer:
**(i)** Draw a right-angled triangle:

- the vertical side is the building, from its foot $B$ up to the window $W$;
- the horizontal side is the ground, from $B$ to the foot of the ladder $F$, with $BF = 5$ m;
- the slanted side $FW$ is the ladder;
- mark the right angle at $B$ and $60^\circ$ at $F$.

**(ii)** $(\alpha)$ $BF$ is adjacent to the $60^\circ$ angle and the ladder is the hypotenuse:

$$\cos 60^\circ = \frac{5}{FW} \implies FW = \frac{5}{\frac{1}{2}} = 10.0 \text{ m}$$

$(\beta)$ $BW$ is opposite the $60^\circ$ angle:

$$\tan 60^\circ = \frac{BW}{5} \implies BW = 5 \times 1.732 = 8.66 \approx 8.7 \text{ m}$$

> [!answer]
> **(i)** Right-angled triangle with base 5 m and $60^\circ$ at the foot of the ladder.
>
> **(ii)** $(\alpha)$ {{green:10.0 m}}  $(\beta)$ {{green:8.7 m}}
